fix: make the Zen summary call satisfy the free-tier fingerprint

Compaction had never reached its summary path: the probe fell back to
truncation and the log said so, but the cause was invisible. Two measured
requirements, both needed at once:

  stream + quartet   200
  stream, no quartet  403
  quartet, no stream  403
  neither             403

The gateway answers "OpenCode's free tier can only be used from within
OpenCode". The summary request was non-streaming and carried no tools, so it
was refused on every oversized session -- exactly the sessions that need it
most. It now streams and reuses applyZenFingerprint, so the quartet and the
tool_choice that keeps the model from calling a tool both come from the same
code path a real turn uses. Frames are reassembled by collectChatStreamText.

Failures now log their reason instead of degrading silently, and two tests pin
the quartet and the reassembly.
